  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Suppose that H ⊆ F1 ⊆ M and H ⊆ F2 ⊆ M where H and M are\nlocal formations of finite groups and F1 is a complement for F2 in the lattice of all\nformations between H and M. Is it true that F1 and F2 are local formations? This is\ntrue in the case H = (1).                                                A. N. Skiba",
